SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later
Subject: Write group 290 header booleans through the boolean encoder

Derived from LibreCAD/libdxfrw 1.0.1, commit
945f2161a13ee521f66f9c52dcfff998e8ccae99, src/drw_header.cpp.
Actual Package CI 38903023174 passes binary magic then fails fileImport
of the unchanged binary roundtrip. Header group 290 is written through
writeInt16 (two binary bytes), but readRec/readBool consumes one byte.
The surplus zero misaligns the next record. Use the existing boolean
writer for all sixteen group 290 header writes; retain values, version
conditions, every other field, ASCII behavior and all tests. Generic
format correction, not a RISC-V workaround. Downstream-only; no upstream
write. Remove when the adopted official release uses boolean-width
serialization for these header flags. Replacement target CI is required.

--- a/src/drw_header.cpp
+++ b/src/drw_header.cpp
@@ -1392,9 +1392,9 @@
             writer->writeInt16(280, 0);
         writer->writeString(9, "$LWDISPLAY"); //RLZ bool flag, verify in bin version
         if (getInt("$LWDISPLAY", &varInt))
-            writer->writeInt16(290, varInt);
-        else
-            writer->writeInt16(290, 0);
+            writer->writeBool(290, varInt);
+        else
+            writer->writeBool(290, 0);
         if (ver > DRW::AC1014) {
             writer->writeString(9, "$INSUNITS");
             if (getInt("$INSUNITS", &varInt))
@@ -1420,9 +1420,9 @@
